; The canonical change from S2 to S3.
;
; S2 |- S3. Change stops being written and starts being derived.
;
; S1 read a codec off a declaration instead of writing one by hand. S3 does
; the same for change: for every declared type there is a change type nobody
; wrote, and `apply`, `diff`, compose and merge are judgments about the schema
; rather than about the type. A change is then an ordinary value, so it
; encodes, it stores and it has an identity.
;
; A semantic change -- what was meant -- elaborates into a structural change
; against the value it is made to, and elaboration is faithful: the change it
; produces is the change that the value it produces would have been diffed
; into.
;
; Laws gain graded evidence, so the system knows which of its claims are
; checked and how. A run over generated values earns `Generated`, and records
; the seed it was drawn from, so it can be had again.
(change
  (kind foundation)
  (name "S2->S3")
  (predecessor (foundation-of "foundations/S2"))
  (delta-meta (file "changes/S2-S3/delta-meta.canon"))
  (delta-grammar (file "changes/S2-S3/delta-grammar.canon"))
  (feature
    (feature
      (name "free changes")
      (programs [
        (file "features/strata/change.generated.meta")
        (file "features/strata/law.generated.meta")
      ])
      (sources [
        (text-file "features/strata/change.meta")
        (text-file "features/strata/law.meta")
        (text-file "strata/lib/change.strata")
        (text-file "strata/lib/law.strata")
      ]))))
